{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T08:40:53.974Z","data":{"text":"Done. All work is complete and `pnpm verify` passes (CLI typecheck, UI typecheck, build, 3724 CLI tests + 152 UI tests, lint).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented task 3 of change 164:\n\n- **`src/core/status/inbox.ts`** — Added `change-archived` to `NeedsYouKind` and made `projectNeedsYou` append one item per `overview.notLanded` entry (`{ kind, change: { id, title }, task: null, command: 'osq land <id>' }`). `readInbox` already sorts needs-you by numeric id, so it needed no change.\n- **`src/core/status/inbox-text.ts`** — `change-archived` rows render as `  <id>: <title> — archived, not landed — osq land <id>`.\n- **`packages/ui/src/home/labels.ts`** — `NEEDS_YOU_LABELS` gains `'change-archived': 'not landed'`.\n- **`README.md`** — the **Needs you** bullet now documents the `vcs.enabled` archived-change case.\n- **`tests/inbox-not-landed.test.ts`** — new coverage building a real temp git repo with a worktree-archived change, before and after merging into `main`, plus the dashboard label and README checks.\n\nI had to keep `src/core/status/inbox.ts` at the 250-line budget: the loop uses a local `command` variable and the `@scenario` tag sits in a one-line JSDoc (noted under `Deviated` in the result).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/164-landed-means-on-main/.run/results/3.md`."}}
